WEBVTT

00:00:09.629 --> 00:00:10.996
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> <b>The Fortune Teller</b>

00:00:11.702 --> 00:00:12.629
<b>Part 1</b>

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:24.592
One night in London, a young police inspector called McCleary had a conversation with his wife.

00:00:25.632 --> 00:00:28.091
"My dear," said McCleary.

00:00:28.604 --> 00:00:32.694
"I can’t stop thinking about our neighbor, Mrs. Myers.

00:00:33.413 --> 00:00:36.375
I’d love to know how she makes her money.

00:00:37.121 --> 00:00:43.763
She lives so luxuriously – she even buys asparagus in the winter!"

00:00:44.624 --> 00:00:47.898
"Leave it to me," said Mrs. McCleary.

00:00:48.625 --> 00:00:50.024
"I have an idea."

00:00:51.324 --> 00:00:54.939
The next day, she dressed like a younger woman,

00:00:55.439 --> 00:01:00.387
took off her wedding ring, and went to visit Mrs. Myers.

00:01:08.871 --> 00:01:13.423
"Sit down, my child," said Mrs. Myers.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.262
"What can I do for you?"

00:01:20.883 --> 00:01:23.151
"I’m going to be 20 tomorrow.

00:01:23.931 --> 00:01:27.959
I want to know what’s going to happen to me in the future."

00:01:29.178 --> 00:01:34.636
Mrs. Myers picked up a deck of cards and began to shuffle them.

00:01:37.323 --> 00:01:39.242
"You are Miss…?"

00:01:39.684 --> 00:01:44.397
"Jones," said Mrs. McCleary, very quietly.

00:01:45.452 --> 00:01:49.771
"My dear Miss Jones," said Mrs. Myers.

00:01:50.451 --> 00:01:56.587
"Please take five cards and put them on the table face down."